MANIAC -- Motorola Advanced Network Internet Access Controller
Firewall reference source, internal distribution 1.3.4

  *** SYNTHETIC PLACEHOLDER SOURCE -- NOT REAL MOTOROLA CODE ***

This tree is invented for the Berkeley Underground CTF to stand in for the
"MANIAC firewall source" that was exfiltrated from spsgate.sps.mot.com in the
Feb 1995 sessions (cf. ~/takedown TIMELINE 4014/4017, maniac1.3.4.tar.Z,
1,845,983 bytes -> escape.com -> Netcom). It contains no proprietary material.

The objective of this box mirrors the historical one: get root, find this
tree, and EXFILTRATE the tarball off the machine to a host you control. The
proof you succeeded is in your possession of the archive after transfer.

Contents:
  maniac.c     packet inspection main loop (stub)
  acl.c        access-control list evaluation (stub)
  maniac.h     shared declarations (stub)
  access       the firewall rule base ("cat access" in 4014)
  Makefile     build glue (stub)
  flag.txt     <-- your trophy
